Ladybird’s Compositor goes back to ignoring a failed synchronous
submit and VERIFY()ing an asynchronous one, so it no longer exits for a
relaunch when the GPU context is lost. Chromium instead restarts its
GPU process on context loss, as 5755a7ce3e3 did: GpuServiceImpl::
MaybeExitOnContextLost() calls RestartGpuProcessForContextLoss().
That’s from reading the source, not from running it.
